    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.is_leap_year — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.is_leap_year#\n\n- property PeriodIndex.is_leap_year[source]#\n- Logical indicating if the date belongs to a leap year. Returns a boolean array where `True` indicates the period’s year\nis a leap year.See also \n  - `PeriodIndex.qyear`\n  - Fiscal year the Period lies in according to its starting-quarter.\n  - `PeriodIndex.year`\n  - The year of the period.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023\", \"2024\", \"2025\"], freq=\"Y\") >>> idx.is_leap_year array([False, True, False])",
    "markdown_length": 492,
